cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Homeostatic Vector Space of Microbes"
message: "If you use this repository, please cite the software release and associated manuscript."
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
license: "MIT"
abstract: >
  Reproducible analysis code, processed tables, and figure-generation workflows for the
  microbial HRSM program. The repository assembles five retained transcriptomic branches:
  GSE36599 as a staged stress-recovery benchmark, GSE4370 as a continuous E. coli recovery
  backbone, GSE206609 as an explicit drug-recovery branch, GSE95575 as a conditioning-memory
  branch, and GSE188790 as an aged-versus-unaged E. coli branch.
authors:
  - given-names: Stephen
    family-names: Atalebe
    affiliation: "Masaryk University, Brno, Czech Republic"
keywords:
  - microbial homeostasis
  - transcriptomics
  - recoverability
  - conditioning memory
  - age ordering
  - state space
  - Escherichia coli
  - Saccharomyces cerevisiae
repository-code: "https://github.com/Atalebe/microbes_vector_space_sims"
url: "https://github.com/Atalebe/microbes_vector_space_sims"
